Q: How can I move a flex-item to the right while two other flex items remain on the left? A: <p><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/flex-grow" rel="nofollow noreferrer">The <code>flex-grow</code> style</a> can help with this.  For example, if the <code>.header</code> element therein increases its <code>flex-grow</code> while leaving the two sibling elements at the default value, that <code>.header</code> element would be more &quot;greedy&quot; when filling up space on the row:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.first-row{
  display: flex;
}

.first-row &gt; .header {
  flex-grow: 2;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="modal"&gt;
  &lt;div class = "first-row"&gt;
    &lt;div class="icon"&gt;!&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="header"&gt;Are you sure you want to do that?&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;button class="close-button"&gt;✖&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt; &lt;!-- Fist Row Div--&gt;
  &lt;div class="text"&gt;Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Pariatur excepturi id soluta, numquam minima rerum doloremque eveniet aspernatur beatae commodi. Cupiditate recusandae ad repellendus quidem consectetur sequi amet aspernatur cumque!&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;button class="continue"&gt;Continue&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button class="cancel"&gt;Cancel&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Appxsym does not contain pdb of exe A: <p>I was able to reproduce the issue with the provided repo and the proper VS setup.</p>
<p>In published .appxsym of Wap project there was indeed only ClassLibrary.pdb .
Was able to force the copy of the AotDemo.pdb using this:</p>
<p>(at the end of .wapproj)</p>
<pre><code>  &lt;Target Name=&quot;AddNativeAotPdbToAppxSym&quot; AfterTargets=&quot;_GenerateAppxSymbolPackage&quot; BeforeTargets=&quot;_CopyAppxSymToOutput&quot;&gt;
    &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
      &lt;_NativeAotPdb&gt;$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\AotDemo\bin\x64\$(Configuration)\net10.0\win-x64\native\AotDemo.pdb&lt;/_NativeAotPdb&gt;
      &lt;_AppxSymPath&gt;$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)obj\x64\$(Configuration)\Symbols\WapProj_1.0.3.0_x64.appxsym&lt;/_AppxSymPath&gt;
      &lt;_AppxSymZip&gt;$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)obj\x64\$(Configuration)\Symbols\WapProj_1.0.3.0_x64.zip&lt;/_AppxSymZip&gt;
    &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;Message Importance=&quot;high&quot; Text=&quot;Adding NativeAOT PDB to appxsym...&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Exec Command=&quot;rename &amp;quot;$(_AppxSymPath)&amp;quot; &amp;quot;WapProj_1.0.3.0_x64.zip&amp;quot;&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Exec Command=&quot;powershell -NoProfile -Command &amp;quot;Compress-Archive -Path '$(_NativeAotPdb)' -DestinationPath '$(_AppxSymZip)' -Update&amp;quot;&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Exec Command=&quot;rename &amp;quot;$(_AppxSymZip)&amp;quot; &amp;quot;WapProj_1.0.3.0_x64.appxsym&amp;quot;&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/Target&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>There's a bit of a hacky list of commands to get the file added due (zip archive...), maybe you can come out with a cleaner one, but after this, I had both pdbs.</p>
<p>Your solution:
I tried to generalize a bit better, check the below with your usecase, if the setup is not too different from your minimal example then this should work:</p>
<pre><code>
  &lt;Target Name=&quot;AddNativeAotPdbToAppxSym&quot; AfterTargets=&quot;_GenerateAppxSymbolPackage&quot; BeforeTargets=&quot;_CopyAppxSymToOutput&quot;&gt;
    &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
      &lt;_EntryPointDir&gt;$([System.IO.Path]::GetDirectoryName('$(EntryPointProjectUniqueName)'))&lt;/_EntryPointDir&gt;
      &lt;_EntryPointName&gt;$([System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension('$(EntryPointProjectUniqueName)'))&lt;/_EntryPointName&gt;
      &lt;_NativeAotPdb&gt;$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)$(_EntryPointDir)\bin\$(Platform)\$(Configuration)\net10.0\$(RuntimeIdentifier)\native\$(_EntryPointName).pdb&lt;/_NativeAotPdb&gt;
      &lt;_SymbolsFolder&gt;$(IntermediateOutputPath)Symbols\&lt;/_SymbolsFolder&gt;
    &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;Exec Command=&quot;powershell -NoProfile -Command &amp;quot;$appxsym = Get-ChildItem '$(_SymbolsFolder)*.appxsym' | Select-Object -First 1; $zip = $appxsym.FullName -replace '\.appxsym$','.zip'; Rename-Item $appxsym.FullName $zip; Compress-Archive -Path '$(_NativeAotPdb)' -DestinationPath $zip -Update; Rename-Item $zip ($zip -replace '\.zip$','.appxsym')&amp;quot;&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Message Importance=&quot;high&quot; Text=&quot;Added NativeAOT PDB to appxsym: $(_EntryPointName).pdb&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/Target&gt;
</code></pre>
